## Docker Day 3 — Volumes & Networking

---

### Why This is Critical for DevOps

Containers have a fundamental problem — they are stateless by default.

When you stop and remove a container — everything inside it is gone. Database records, uploaded files, log files — all deleted. In production this is a disaster.

Another problem — containers need to talk to each other. Your web app container needs to reach your database container. Your nginx container needs to forward requests to your application container.

**Volumes solve the data problem. Networking solves the communication problem. Both are essential for real applications.**

